  "title": "JuiceFS vs ObjectiveFS",
  "summary": "Compares JuiceFS and ObjectiveFS, two POSIX-compatible filesystems built on object storage, focusing on their architectural tradeoffs, metadata handling, operational overhead, and consistency models. Helps teams decide whether they prefer an open, operator-managed system or a fully managed filesystem with stronger built-in guarantees and simpler operations.",
